    <string name="info_button">About this screen</string>
    <string name="info_heading_what">What it is</string>
    <string name="info_heading_does">What it does</string>
    <string name="info_heading_how">How it works</string>
    <string name="info_got_it">Got it</string>
    <string name="info_owner_title">Device owner</string>
    <string name="info_restrictions_what">System-level rules for the whole phone, like blocking factory reset or app installs.</string>
    <string name="info_restrictions_does">Lets you switch on Android\'s built-in restrictions, which Déchaîner can enforce because it\'s the device owner.</string>
    <string name="info_restrictions_how">Each switch is a real Android policy, so the phone itself refuses the action. No app can bypass it. Recommended ones are listed first.</string>
    <string name="info_apps_what">Suspend any app with one switch, or give it a daily time limit.</string>
    <string name="info_apps_does">The switch pauses an app right now: greyed out, unopenable, notifications hidden. Tap an app to set a daily limit; when the time is up it is paused until midnight.</string>
    <string name="info_apps_how">Android itself suspends apps, because Déchaîner is the device owner. Limits use Android\'s own usage log, read only while the phone is awake, plus a non-wakeup alarm for the earliest moment a limit could run out: no service, no polling, no wake-ups from sleep. Needs Usage access once. Lifting a suspension takes your recovery code, and an app held by a schedule, a block or a limit stays held until it ends.</string>
    <string name="info_config_what">Settings for Déchaîner itself and its protections.</string>
    <string name="info_config_does">Private DNS, protections, entry challenge, recovery code, unlock delay, keyboard type and forced removal.</string>
    <string name="info_config_how">Anything that weakens protection goes through your recovery code, and through the unlock delay if you\'ve set one. Forced removal is the escape hatch: it lifts everything after a 4-day wait, without the code.</string>
    <string name="info_schedules_what">Weekly block windows, plus Study mode.</string>
    <string name="info_schedules_does">A schedule suspends chosen apps, system features and websites at set times every week. With \"allow only\" on, it flips around: only the apps you list work. Duplicate a schedule, or copy apps from another, so you don\'t pick them twice.</string>
    <string name="info_schedules_how">An exact alarm wakes Déchaîner at each window\'s start and end. Nothing polls in the background, so it costs almost no battery. Automatic time is always forced, so changing the clock can\'t skip a window. \"Lock while active\" makes a running window uneditable.</string>
    <string name="info_entry_what">A small challenge in front of Déchaîner itself, for moments when you want to undo your own rules.</string>
    <string name="info_entry_does">Adds a challenge (math or typing) before the app opens. It does not lock anything by itself.</string>
    <string name="info_entry_how">The challenge runs after authentication, every time you open Déchaîner.</string>
    <string name="info_owner_what">The permission that makes blocking real.</string>
    <string name="info_owner_does">Makes Déchaîner the device owner, which lets it suspend apps, apply system restrictions, and stop itself from being uninstalled.</string>
    <string name="info_owner_how">Granted once via ADB or Shizuku during setup. Android only allows one device owner at a time.</string>
